{title: The Wild Rover}
{artist: Traditional Irish}
{key: G}
{tempo: 126}
{time: 3/4}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: folk, irish, pub}
{comment: In the chorus, clap four times after "no, nay, never".}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I've been a [G]wild rover for [G]many a [C]year [C]
And I've [G]spent all my [G]money on [D]whiskey and [D]beer
But [G]now I'm re[G]turning with [C]gold in great [C]store
And I [G]never will [D]play the wild [G]rover no [G]more

{start_of_chorus}
And it's [D]no, nay, never [D]
[G]No, nay, never no [C]more
Will I [G]play the wild [C]rover
No [D]never, no [G]more

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I [G]went to an [G]alehouse I [C]used to fre[C]quent
And I [G]told the land[G]lady my [D]money was [D]spent
I [G]asked her for [G]credit, she [C]answered me [C]"Nay,
Such a [G]custom as [D]yours I could [G]have any [G]day."
